{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-monoidal-functor","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-monoidal-functor","kind":"remark","title":"Monoidal functor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-monoidal-category"],"tags":["glossary","category-theory","monoidal"],"defines":["monoidal-functor"],"text":"glossary-monoidal-functor.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-monoidal-functor\"></a><p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-monoidal-functor\">Monoidal functor</dfn>.</strong> A functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F \\colon \\mathbf{C} \\to \\mathbf{D}</code> between monoidal categories equipped with a natural transformation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu_{X,Y} \\colon F(X) \\otimes F(Y) \\to F(X \\otimes Y)</code> and a morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon \\colon \\mathbf{1}_{\\mathbf{D}} \\to F(\\mathbf{1}_{\\mathbf{C}})</code>. These are compatible with the associator and unitors.</p>\n<p>The functor is <em>lax</em> monoidal when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon</code> are arbitrary morphisms and <em>strong</em> monoidal when they are isomorphisms.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-monoidal-functor.md","heading":"Remark","number":"30.2.5","page":"b/rem-glossary-monoidal-functor","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
